cFS is used unmodified; Ping Lite adds separate apps and mission definition
files that are overlaid onto a scratch copy at build time (scripts/build_cfs.sh).

Use of cFS does not imply NASA endorsement of Ping Lite. "NASA" and "cFS" are
used only to identify the upstream software.

The optional ISSLive adapter (sim/plsim/isslive.py) reads the public ISS
telemetry feed relayed by Lightstreamer; item identifiers are taken from the
ISS-Mimic project (https://github.com/ISS-Mimic/Mimic). No code is copied from
either project.
